-aligned gauge cancels the mixed matter–color quadratic term. The bounded magnetic correction leaves a color-normal squared-frequency gap &gt;aN/16 and an unused-vacuum gap &gt;3aN/32. In a=N=1 these frequencies exceed the slow radial frequency by factors of 20 and 25. Twenty saddle embeddings retain their scalar instabilities. Twenty-eight exact/interval checks and four synthetic matrix fixtures passed. Oscillators precede the residual stabilizer constraint and quotient. The interval is sufficient; an explicit nonlinear perturbation radius remains open. Independent review pending; physical promotion 0.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/sources/finite-rank-v0.1/UD_FULL_RANK_FINITE_OFFSET_STABILITY_v0.1.pdf">Read theorem PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/finite-rank-v0.1/UD_FULL_RANK_FINITE_OFFSET_STABILITY_v0.1_RELEASE.zip">Theorem and verification package ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=FRC01">Claims and scope →</a></div></div></article><article class="paper-row" id="finite-offset-v01"><div class="paper-number">G12</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Computer-assisted conditional theorem · development 0.1</span><h2>An explicit finite-offset region is certified</h2><p>All 26 labeled phase branches continue throughout 0&lt;ε≤10⁻⁵, with ε=κ/(rN)−k*. A 44-variable analytic rescaling removes the threshold singularity.</p><p class="muted">The relative radius-squared error is at most 25ε, fast-loop error at most 297ε³ᐟ², and six-real-loop classifier bias at most 41ε. Explicit phase and real-channel noise budgets guarantee class discrimination. In a=N=r=1, the soft-mode frequency ratio stays within 0.005 of its limiting value. Three global boxes, 1,536 nested interval boxes and 2,048 spectral cut tests passed. Stationary embeddings and readout bounds apply at every finite rank; full-rank finite-offset stability of the minima remains open. Independent review pending; physical promotion 0.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button 