+# FRC v0.1 — finite-offset full-rank stability
+
+Under the unchanged candidate action, all six balanced one-active-color phase-branch embeddings are nonlinearly orbitally stable at every fixed finite rank throughout 0<epsilon<=10^-5, epsilon=kappa/(r*N)-k_star. The twelve index-one and eight index-two scalar saddle embeddings remain unstable. At epsilon=0 the balanced branches coalesce at the inherited quartically stable critical orbit.
+
+The exact cancellation in a matter-aligned gauge removes the mixed matter–color Hessian term. A two-color determinant identity bounds the magnetic normal correction by the diamond phase. The one-color normal energy is bounded below by a||e||^2+(17/10)||Q||^2+(N/16)||beta||^2; its stronger link margin is 2599*N/40000. The linear color squared-frequency gap exceeds a*N/16 and the unused-block vacuum gap exceeds 3*a*N/32. In a=N=1 their frequency ratios to the slow radial mode exceed 20 and 25 respectively.
+
+Constructor verification: 28 exact/rigorous interval checks plus four floating full-matrix synthetic diagnostics. Seven PDF pages rendered, decoded and visually inspected. Oscillators are on the linear symplectic slice before the residual moment-map constraint and quotient. No explicit nonlinear basin radius, sharp outer coefficient boundary, independent review or physical correspondence. Development, no registry entry. Physical promotion 0.
